# {{ .ModuleType }}

This is a README for your module. Feel free to edit it.

## Quickstart

The module builds as soon as it is created — `dagger_sdk/` is seeded for you.
To give it bindings generated from your own engine's schema:

```console
$ dagger generate
```

That rewrites `dagger_sdk/` — commit it. The module runtime builds from those
sources and never regenerates them.

## The project structure

The module is a regular cargo project:

```text
.
├── .cargo
│   └── config.toml
├── dagger_sdk
├── src
│   └── main.rs
├── Cargo.toml
└── README.md
```

`src/main.rs` is the module source. `dagger_sdk` is written by `dagger generate`:
it holds the Dagger Rust SDK together with the API bindings generated from your
engine's schema.

`.cargo/config.toml` is not optional. The module is `no_std` and links without
libc or a dynamic loader — [goish](https://github.com/cogentica-ai/goish)
provides `_start` and the runtime itself — so the flags there are what make the
binary link at all.

## Status

The Rust SDK is a scaffold. `dagger module init`, `dagger generate` and the
module build all work, but the SDK cannot yet talk to the engine: the example
functions in `src/main.rs` are not registered, and running the module exits with
a message saying so. Treat this as a starting point for the SDK, not a working
module.
